# What each of Polish's own characters arrives as: the code point a caller
# writes, and the byte its alphabet knows that character by. The bytes are the
# ones lang-alphabet.py put the letters at, which were free in the alphabet
# Italian brought; tools/lang-alphabet.py show plpl says what each one is now.

0105 82   # a with ogonek
0107 83   # c with acute
0119 84   # e with ogonek
0142 86   # l with stroke
0144 87   # n with acute
015b 88   # s with acute
017a 89   # z with acute
017c 8b   # z with dot above

0104 8d   # and the capitals
0106 8e
0118 8f
0141 90
0143 91
015a 92
0179 9b
017b 9e
